WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.375 --> 00:00:04.325
Unit twenty-one. Nosebleeds and Small Injuries!

2
00:00:05.304 --> 00:00:09.087
Hello, everyone! I'm Nurse Bopha, your school nurse.

3
00:00:09.137 --> 00:00:12.671
Hi, Nurse Bopha! What do we learn today?

4
00:00:12.722 --> 00:00:17.290
Today we learn about Nosebleeds and Small Injuries. Let's go!

5
00:00:18.018 --> 00:00:21.635
Nosebleed. Say it with me. Nosebleed!

6
00:00:25.121 --> 00:00:29.088
Lean forward. Say it with me. Lean forward!

7
00:00:32.585 --> 00:00:35.935
Pinch. Say it with me. Pinch!

8
00:00:39.453 --> 00:00:42.786
Bruise. Say it with me. Bruise!

9
00:00:46.293 --> 00:00:49.409
Cut. Say it with me. Cut!

10
00:00:52.882 --> 00:00:56.065
Clean. Say it with me. Clean!

11
00:00:59.575 --> 00:01:02.991
Bandage. Say it with me. Bandage!

12
00:01:06.475 --> 00:01:10.142
Adult. Say it with me. Adult!

13
00:01:13.641 --> 00:01:23.301
For a nosebleed, sit, lean forward, and pinch the soft part of the nose. Clean a cut and cover it with a bandage. A bruise may need a cold pack, and an adult can help.

14
00:01:23.351 --> 00:01:24.538
I can do that too!

15
00:01:25.904 --> 00:01:31.201
Look! What's the word?

16
00:01:31.251 --> 00:01:32.401
Pinch!

17
00:01:33.196 --> 00:01:38.625
Look! What's the word?

18
00:01:38.675 --> 00:01:39.825
Bandage!

19
00:01:40.689 --> 00:01:46.438
Did you know? Leaning back during a nosebleed can make blood run down your throat!

20
00:01:46.488 --> 00:01:48.434
Wow! I did not know that!

21
00:01:49.123 --> 00:01:57.469
Think and answer. Why should you lean forward, not back, in a nosebleed?

22
00:01:57.519 --> 00:01:58.669
Great answer!

23
00:01:59.918 --> 00:02:04.610
Great job today! Stay healthy, and see you next time. Goodbye!

24
00:02:04.660 --> 00:02:07.174
Goodbye, everyone! Stay healthy!

